  "body": "## What this changes\n\nDraft, as agreed: the MTP verify windows batched across streams in the lanes engine, with the same bit-for-bit contract. Is the \"CUDA per-stream drafting precision\" work on #286 touching `cuda_mtp_ops.zig` / `verifyFn` too? If so, I'll rebase this onto it rather than collide.\n\n`verifyFn` ran one batched pass per drafting stream, so a round over N streams read the weights N times and the aggregate stayed flat (81.8, 70.3 and 64.0 tok/s at 1, 2 and 4 streams on a GB10, code prompt, `--parallel 4`). Now the drafted windows of a round share one pass, up to the round's 64 rows (`TF_FLASHNEXT_WINDOW_ROWS`, 0 keeps each window alone; never past `TF_FLASHNEXT_CHUNK`).\n\n- `batch.Lane` gains a row span and the lane's own rollback (`keep`), hidden-row (`streams`) and score (`logits`) destinations. `rows = 1` and none of them is the one-row round as before, which keeps its launches. A lane's `keep` may hold a window's DeltaNet rollback only (`rollbackOnly`); a training pass's kept tensors are refused, as the round already refuses `moe_add`.\n- Per lane, with the row count and launches its lone pass makes: n-gram gather, media inject, PLE convolution and tail, DeltaNet front, chain (to the lane's kept state) and conv shift, attention (rope, cache writes, pooling, indexer scores, selection, chunks).\n- Once over all rows: the matmuls, hyper-connection blocks, router, experts and head. An untaught stream's rows read no pocket, as in `round`.\n- `Engine.windows` (`cuda_prompt_windows.zig`) runs the pass. `Ops.verifyMany` refuses every window before any stream's state moves, then leaves each stream as its `verify` leaves it (saved tail and PLE rows, host scores row, `fed`). `verifyFn` groups the drafted windows (`cuda_lanes_verify.zig`). Plain one-row rounds and two ranks keep their paths (two ranks would need one wire command for the batch).\n\n2 commits, 16 files, +376/-48, all in `zig/src/families/flashnext/` (`cuda_batch*.zig`, `cuda_prompt*.zig`, `cuda_mtp_ops.zig`, `cuda_lanes*.zig`, `cuda_round_graph.zig`, which refuses a window it never captures, `cuda_media.zig` and two test row types) and `zig/tests/cuda/` (`flashnext_windows_tests.zig`, `main.zig`).\n\n## Receipt\n\n- Environment: TensorFold main `d1018b31` + this branch; NVIDIA DGX Spark, GB10 sm_121, driver 595.84, nvcc 13.2.86; checkpoint Flash Next MLX 4-bit with MTP (`qwen4_exp`), drafts on (depth 6, confidence 0.6), `--context 32768 --parallel 4`, chunk 16384.\n- Exactness:\n  - new `tf-cuda-test flashnext-windows MODEL IDS`: several streams' forced windows in one shared pass against each window alone, on a 100-token and a 2,600-token prompt (the indexer's sparse selection), windows of {1,1,1,1}, {5,5,5,5}, {1,16,3,7}, {16,16} and {16,16,16,16} rows (4 to 64 in all; past 16 rows the router takes its many-row kernel, which a lone window never reaches): each window's scores, hidden rows and last host row, then after a partial rollback the position, n-gram history and next row, byte for byte: 10 of 10 pass. With every lane reading the first lane's position it fails (`124152 of 124160 words differ`).\n  - `bench_concurrent.py --alone --serial`, levels 1/2/4, T=0 (2 reps) and T=1: 0 unequal, 0 failed; at T=0 the same `token_sha256` per prompt and level as with `TF_FLASHNEXT_WINDOW_ROWS=0`. At `--parallel 2 --context 131072`, levels 1/4, 3 reps: 0 unequal.\n- Aggregate tok/s, 512 tokens each, same binary with `TF_FLASHNEXT_WINDOW_ROWS=0` (each window alone, main's path) and the default:\n\n  | prompt | T | 1 stream, alone / shared | 4 streams, alone | 4 streams, shared | |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n  | code | 0 | 80.9 / 80.5 | 79.9 | 134.0 | x1.68 |\n  | chat | 0 | 66.1 / 65.6 | 68.1 | 122.4 | x1.80 |\n  | French prose | 0 | 55.0 / 55.0 | 57.1 | 105.9 | x1.85 |\n  | JSON list | 0 | 82.5 / 82.7 | 82.6 | 140.3 | x1.70 |\n  | code | 1 | 71.3 / 71.6 | 75.0 | 120.1 | x1.60 |\n  | chat | 1 | 60.2 / 60.5 | 62.4 | 104.0 | x1.67 |\n  | French prose | 1 | 71.7 / 71.8 | 69.0 | 109.8 | x1.59 |\n  | JSON list | 1 | 82.2 / 82.2 | 80.5 | 130.6 | x1.62 |\n\n  Tokens per round are unchanged (the drafts and their acceptance are the same). `bench_openai.py` at `--parallel 2 --context 131072`, one stream: fibonacci-raw 81.7, gpu-chat-no-think 69.4 tok/s.\n- Prompt speed: n/a, prompt chunks do not go through the shared verify.\n- Tests run: `zig fmt --check`, `native`, `test`, `test-kernel-contract`, `test-golden`, `fuzz-cortheon`, `test-cuda-host` pass; lean check 444 problems (main's count); `tf-cuda-test` smoke, symbols, route-rows, experts-rows, flashnext-hc, flashnext-attn, flashnext-dense-hc, flashnext-draft-affine, flashnext-shared, flashnext-nvfp4-tp, norms, norm-rows, sample, projection-f32, mxfp8, quant-ref, modelopt, glue, glm-ref and flashnext-windows pass; `kernel-contract` `SUMMARY 85 kernels: 85 pass gates 1-4, 0 fail, 0 known findings; 7 controls: 7 red as planted, 0 missed; 899 limit problems`, the same 899 lines as main at `d1018b31` (no kernel changes here).\n- Not run, and why:\n  - Two ranks: unchanged path; Flash Next's two-rank CUDA loader takes its ranks from `--tp`, which the CUDA build does not serve.\n  - A taught pocket (Living Weights) with a shared verify: no taught checkpoint here; the shared pass follows `round`'s per-row pocket scales.\n  - Metal: no Mac here, no Metal file touched.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Every token still goes through the lane rounds. No serial path, and nothing that needs drafts off.\n- [x] Drafted output equals `\"draft\": false`, a resumed prompt equals a fresh one (prompt passes are untouched), and concurrent equals solo.\n- [x] No precision traded for speed. The bits do not change.\n- [x] No GPU kernel is new or changed (the shared pass launches the existing ones).\n- [x] Prompt processing is no slower than the last release (not reached).\n- [x] CUDA GB10 run; Metal not run (no Mac, no Metal file touched).\n- [x] New tests fail before the change, pass after it, and skip cleanly without their dependency: the shared verify does not exist before it, so the receipt shows the test failing on a planted per-lane position bug; `flashnext-windows` needs the checkpoint, like `flashnext-window-rank`.\n- [x] Comments and docstrings are one line. No measurements or history in the source.\n- [x] No personal data, machine names, internal hosts or local paths. No AI attribution lines.\n",
